# Parser cases for hosted-parser-test; expected output is golden/hosted_parser.golden
# (hosted-parser-test --update CASES GOLDEN rewrites it for review).
#
# '#' lines are comments and blank lines are ignored.
#   @case NAME            one case; its following lines are the source, joined by newlines
#   @cases LABEL          one case per following line, named "LABEL[/VARIANT] LINE"
#   @variant NAME [P|S]   (in @cases) also run each line as P + LINE + S; \n, \r, \t in P/S
#   @step MODE OPTION...  parse step of the current case or variant, in order
# In @cases, a @variant or @step after source lines starts a new configuration.
# Modes: expr, body, type, callable, field, preamble, enum (Aurora grammar entries),
# program and parser (the whole-source lex, parse and admission entry of the resolver
# and formatter), resolve (whole module through typed lowering), raw (the private
# parser ABI record, every copied record and optional admission). Diagnostics are
# rendered as the compiler renders them; records print as expression and type trees
# and one line per syntax row, and a dump over 64 lines as its line count and digest.
# Options: stop=NAME, at=N|snippet|next|^K (token ordinal, first token of the line inside
# its variant wrapper, cursor after the previous successful step, or the K-th marker),
# types=A,B caps=N fn (captured template context, by first token of that spelling),
# count=N (enum count), and for raw: offset=N rawctx=W,... admit config=W,... reuse.
# The marker character U+2038 is removed from the source and records a position.
# «N|TEXT» in a source line is N copies of TEXT, «N,|TEXT» joins them with commas,
# and '#' in TEXT is the copy ordinal; case names keep the unexpanded line.

# ---- Expressions: every operator, postfix, aggregate, template and reflection form.
@cases expr
@variant semicolon |;
@step expr
1
123u64
255u8
false
true
name
